// A CHAINED `.map` whose inner callback returns `i64`. `vl check` returns 0 and the emitter
// refuses with `emitProgram: .map/.filter over i64[] but i64 list type not collected`
// (`compiler/wasmEmit.vl:17390`). Should print 2.
//
// SAME MECHANISM AS `map-callback-f32-indexed-assign.vl`: `collectMapFilterUse`
// (`emit_collect.vl:12800-12807`) has an `f64` arm and an i32 default and no `i64` / `f32` /
// `u8` arm, so the inner map yields an i64-repped list with `ia64Used` false.
//
// THE CHAIN MUST BE ONE EXPRESSION, and that is a real property of the witness rather than
// styling. Bind the inner map to its own `const` and the INNER call's destination floor
// (`.map result is i64[] but i64 list type not collected`, `wasmEmit.vl:17442`) is recorded
// first — `emitFail` keeps only the first message — and masks this site entirely. Chained, the
// outer `emitMapFilter`'s source ladder runs before the receiver is emitted.
//
// That masking is the general hazard this whole measurement had to work around: a program can
// reach a site and report a different site's sentence.
function toI(n: i32): i64 { return 5 as! i64 }
function idI(n: i64): i64 { return n }
function main() {
  const xs = [1, 2]
  const zs = xs.map(toI).map(idI)
  print(zs.length)
}
main()
